  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Modern Islamic Thinking and Activism shows clear signs of use rather than citation-led scholarly uptake at this stage. The strongest signal is sustained readership, with 3,350 OAPEN downloads, alongside open-access availability that makes the book readily accessible to researchers and students. The record also shows no indexed citations in OpenAlex, so its impact is currently better described through access and use than through formal citation accumulation.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Published by Leuven University Press in 2014, Modern Islamic Thinking and Activism is framed around Islamic thinking, activism, and politics in Western and Middle Eastern contexts. Its subject profile sits at the intersection of Islam, political science, sociology, and history, reflecting a work intended to support comparative and interdisciplinary inquiry rather than a narrowly bounded disciplinary audience.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The clearest evidence of impact in the record is readership. OAPEN metrics report 3,350 downloads, indicating steady use of the book in an open-access environment. The monthly pattern suggests ongoing engagement over time rather than a single isolated surge, which is consistent with a scholarly book being consulted for research, teaching preparation, or background reading.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Open-access availability likely supports that reach. OpenAIRE identifies the book as available in hybrid open access with open instances recorded, including the publisher-hosted version and an OAPEN copy. That kind of distribution lowers barriers to access and can widen the pool of potential readers, particularly in fields where books often circulate through libraries and course-related use.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The broader scholarly citation record is still quiet: OpenAlex reports 0 citations for this work. That does not diminish the book\u2019s apparent use, but it does mean that its documented influence is, at present, more visible in download activity and repository access than in formal citation uptake. Teaching-related holdings are also present through WorldCat, which suggests library discoverability and possible instructional use, though the digest does not provide course-listing evidence.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the record depicts a book with measurable readership and strong access infrastructure, but limited captured citation evidence so far. In impact terms, it is best understood as a work with established availability and demonstrable consultation, while its longer-term scholarly afterlife in citations may still be developing.</p>",
